# The two authority registers are machine-maintained by
# scripts/console/rebind-authority-train.mjs. Measured on 2026-07-28: a routine
# authority commit changes 780 lines across them, and 780 of 780 contain a SHA —
# zero are semantic. That noise buries the reviewable content of every PR (891
# lines total vs 111 once these two are set aside).
#
# `linguist-generated` collapses them to one expandable line in GitHub's diff,
# where review actually happens. Nothing is hidden: a reviewer can expand on
# demand. This is deliberately NOT `-diff`, which would render them as binary and
# make the real content unviewable.
#
# CI is unaffected — verified. Nothing textually diffs these files:
# validate-console-truth-ledger.mjs reads them with `git show <sha>:path`, and
# verify-console-authority-train.mjs uses `git diff --raw --no-ext-diff`, which
# reports mode/SHA/status only. `linguist-generated` is a GitHub rendering hint
# and does not change local git behaviour at all.
#
# Considered and rejected: stripping the SHA leaves from the registers. It was
# refuted four times — it weakens the merge gate at three sites covering 91% of
# the leaves, because those `?.candidate_sha` comparisons double as existence
# checks. See docs/ideas/process-minimum-viable-provenance.md.
docs/program/console-capability-registry.json    linguist-generated=true
docs/program/console-jurisdiction-register.json  linguist-generated=true
